    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51197" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰσοφᾰρίζω</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῑ]</span>,= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιφερίζω</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>match oneself with, vie with</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδέ τίς οἱ δύναται μένος
					ἰσοφαρίζειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					6.101
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔργα δ᾽ Ἀθηναίῃ . . ἰσοφαρίζοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					9.390
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μνήμην οὔτινά φημι Σιμωνίδῃ
					-φαρίζειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Simon.
					146
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				7.30
			</span></i>: generally, <i>to be equal to</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινι</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				21.194
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				490
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> trans.,
				<i>make equal</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				572
			</span></i>.</div>
